1
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:08,352
Good evening.

2
00:00:08,372 --> 00:00:10,256
I trust you had a fruitful day.

3
00:00:10,516 --> 00:00:13,201
I do not say happy, though I hope it has been happy.

4
00:00:13,221 --> 00:00:22,097
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambhodasa.

5
00:00:22,117 --> 00:00:29,751
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambhodasa.

6
00:00:30,507 --> 00:00:45,225
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambho Tassa Homage to the Buddha, the Blessed Noble and fully self-awakened one.

7
00:00:45,246 --> 00:00:46,667
So no hitch tonight.

8
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:52,854
We're going to get into the habit of rebooting the Ruta every week.

9
00:00:53,676 --> 00:00:56,700
So that should stop the problem I had last night.

10
00:00:57,963 --> 00:01:08,197
So now there comes a point in the discourses where there's a natural repetition of the teachings.

11
00:01:09,721 --> 00:01:19,715
Not only is there repetition within the discourse itself, but there's also throughout the discourses a repetition of the teachings.

12
00:01:19,936 --> 00:01:23,802
There's always something new added and a little nuance, you might say.

13
00:01:25,503 --> 00:01:28,727
So this is the discourse on the cowherd.

14
00:01:29,709 --> 00:01:30,891
It's number 33.

15
00:01:32,534 --> 00:01:40,466
And the Buddha is at Anathapindika's park again up in Savatthi, probably his most favourite place.

16
00:01:41,569 --> 00:01:47,037
And he's talking to the monks or to the people who are listening.

17
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:55,209
When a cow herd possesses 11 factors, he is incapable of keeping and rearing a herd of cattle.

18
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:56,611
What 11?

19
00:01:57,132 --> 00:02:00,376
Here, a cow herd has no knowledge of form.

20
00:02:01,218 --> 00:02:03,480
He is unskillful in characteristics.

21
00:02:04,182 --> 00:02:06,584
He fails to pick out the fly's eggs.

22
00:02:07,605 --> 00:02:09,288
He fails to dress the wounds.

23
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:12,451
He fails to smoke out the sheds.

24
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:15,204
He does not know the watering place.

25
00:02:15,985 --> 00:02:18,468
He does not know what it is to have drunk.

26
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:20,992
He does not know the road.

27
00:02:21,453 --> 00:02:23,376
He's unskilled in pastures.

28
00:02:23,956 --> 00:02:25,519
He milks dry.

29
00:02:25,538 --> 00:02:32,088
And he shows no extra veneration to those bulls who are the fathers and leaders of the herd.

30
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:37,737
So these are the skills you need when you become a cowherd, okay?

31
00:02:39,941 --> 00:02:41,443
Don't all rush out now.

32
00:02:42,217 --> 00:02:51,288
So now, of course, he uses these metaphors in order to talk about the Dharma.

33
00:02:51,308 --> 00:02:56,796
So he says all that about people who are striving, shall we say.

34
00:02:57,858 --> 00:03:03,225
So here, remember, every time I say Bhikkhu, it means anybody who's striving.

35
00:03:03,586 --> 00:03:06,250
How has a Bhikkhu no knowledge of form?

36
00:03:06,787 --> 00:03:18,384
Here he does not understand that it actually is all material form in whatever kind consists of the four great elements and the material form derived from the four great elements.

37
00:03:18,485 --> 00:03:25,396
So we're talking about what we would normally call matter, the body and what it's made of.

38
00:03:25,437 --> 00:03:32,608
Now remember these four great elements as they're called, earth, fire, water and air,

39
00:03:34,799 --> 00:03:47,306
solidity, fluidity, elasticity, heat, cold and movement.

40
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:50,421
That's how we contact matter.

41
00:03:50,883 --> 00:03:52,144
So it's not what matter is.

42
00:03:52,204 --> 00:03:54,825
We know it's chemicals and subatomic particles and all that.

43
00:03:55,105 --> 00:03:57,168
It's how the mind contacts matter.

44
00:03:57,868 --> 00:04:02,111
And he doesn't know it, this poor striver, or a real striver.

45
00:04:03,133 --> 00:04:06,235
And of course, everything is derived from that.

46
00:04:06,795 --> 00:04:09,739
In other words, that's at the base of all our experience.

47
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,502
He doesn't know form, you see.

48
00:04:14,923 --> 00:04:17,125
How is him skilled in the characteristics?

49
00:04:17,694 --> 00:04:25,947
He does not understand as it actually is, a fool is characterized by their action and a wise person characterized by their actions.

50
00:04:26,588 --> 00:04:30,355
Can't tell the difference between a foolish person and a wise person.

51
00:04:32,117 --> 00:04:34,961
How does he fail to pick out the fly's eggs?

52
00:04:35,701 --> 00:04:39,766
When a thought of sensual desire arises, the bhikkhu tolerates it.

53
00:04:40,185 --> 00:04:44,310
He does not abandon it, remove it, do away with it, annihilate it.

54
00:04:44,891 --> 00:04:48,716
And the same with thoughts of ill will and the same with thoughts of cruelty.

55
00:04:49,838 --> 00:04:50,879
So he's not quick.

56
00:04:50,939 --> 00:04:56,805
So a person who, when these thoughts come, are not quick to acknowledge it and say, I see you, Mara, you see?

57
00:04:56,865 --> 00:04:58,988
Therefore not picking out the fly's eggs.

58
00:05:00,129 --> 00:05:01,711
And therefore you're left with a wound.

59
00:05:02,252 --> 00:05:05,016
How does he fail to dress the wounds?

60
00:05:05,165 --> 00:05:32,083
on seeing form with the eye a vehicle grasps at its signs and features right gets gets attached to it even though when he leaves the eye faculty unguarded evil unwholesome states of covetousness and grief might invade him he does not practice the way of its restraint he does not guard the eye faculty he does not understate undertake the restraint of the eye faculties in other words

61
00:05:32,232 --> 00:05:39,781
Remember, every act of attention is an act of intention, and therefore it is conditioning, right?

62
00:05:41,204 --> 00:05:47,973
So once we've grasped that, every time we attend to something and we see it's unwholesome, we have to guard that sense.

63
00:05:48,053 --> 00:05:49,134
We mustn't put it there.

64
00:05:49,615 --> 00:05:50,757
I must take it away.

65
00:05:51,458 --> 00:05:58,627
And that also means knowing not where to go, not where to look, even before you see it, you might say.

66
00:06:04,935 --> 00:06:12,767
So in this way, he leaves the faculty that all these faculties unguarded and evil, unwholesome states of covetous and grief and grief.

67
00:06:13,608 --> 00:06:22,762
That's that's the usual indulgence and aversion invade him.

68
00:06:23,084 --> 00:06:27,771
So, OK, how does Abiku fail to smoke out the sheds?

69
00:06:28,055 --> 00:06:33,620
Here he does not teach others in detail the Dharma as he has learnt it and mastered it.

70
00:06:34,259 --> 00:06:45,170
So anytime there's an opportunity for us to teach the meditation or to tell somebody about the meditation or the practice of Buddhism, then we ought to do so.

71
00:06:45,870 --> 00:06:49,553
Failing to do so is a lost opportunity.

72
00:06:50,375 --> 00:06:57,740
I'm not so sure how that fits in with smoking out the sheds, but I'm sure one of you will email me.

73
00:06:58,598 --> 00:07:03,343
Anyway, that's called smoking out the sheds.

74
00:07:03,723 --> 00:07:05,605
He does not know the watering place.

75
00:07:07,146 --> 00:07:18,278
Now, a bhikkhu does not go from time to time to those bhikkhus who blurt much, who are well versed in the tradition, who maintain the dharma, the discipline and the codes.

76
00:07:18,759 --> 00:07:21,442
And he does not inquire and ask questions of him thus.

77
00:07:22,182 --> 00:07:23,463
How is this, Venerable Sir?

78
00:07:23,603 --> 00:07:25,146
What is the meaning of this?

79
00:07:25,396 --> 00:07:36,230
These venerables do not reveal in him what has not been revealed, do not clarify what is not clear, or remove his doubts about numerous things that give rise to doubts.

80
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:53,951
So in other words, he's not going to certain peoples or places, or in our terms, to books and reading and audios and other teachers to refine

81
00:07:54,218 --> 00:07:57,742
our understanding of the Dharma and, of course, our practice.

82
00:08:00,625 --> 00:08:03,767
The Dharma is both the understanding and the practice.

83
00:08:03,807 --> 00:08:07,531
The discipline and codes is, of course, our moral conduct.

84
00:08:09,514 --> 00:08:13,057
How does a bhikkhu not know what it is to have drunk?

85
00:08:15,259 --> 00:08:21,947
When the Dharma and the discipline proclaimed by the targetter is being taught, the bhikkhu does not gain inspiration.

86
00:08:22,264 --> 00:08:41,015
the meaning does not gain inspiration in the dharma does not grain gladness connected to the dharma so when we are when we're practicing and we're no longer feeling inspired no matter how what level it is it might be it might be just you know point one um

87
00:08:41,332 --> 00:08:47,783
You know, once we begin to lose inspiration, then of course we lose interest and the practice goes aside.

88
00:08:48,203 --> 00:08:55,115
So in a sense, we've got to read, we've got to practice to keep inspiring ourselves, keep encouraging ourselves to do that practice.

89
00:08:59,101 --> 00:09:00,705
How does a bhikkhu not know the road?

90
00:09:01,265 --> 00:09:05,272
Here a bhikkhu does not understand the eight bone noble path as it actually is.

91
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:08,116
Okay, so you know that.

92
00:09:08,822 --> 00:09:31,000
because unskilled in pastures here a big who does not understand the four foundations of mindfulness as they actually are so we did that when we did the four foundations of mindfulness um in the this discourse number 10 on how to establish mindfulness so remember that was mindfulness of the body mindfulness of feelings

93
00:09:37,831 --> 00:09:39,716
Seven factors of enlightenment.

94
00:09:43,105 --> 00:09:43,767
Pastures.

95
00:09:44,207 --> 00:09:46,113
It's often talked about the pastures.

96
00:09:46,634 --> 00:09:54,355
Pastures is used in the scriptures to mean where you should put your attention on these pastures.

97
00:09:57,337 --> 00:09:59,320
How does a bhikkhu milk dry?

98
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:10,412
When faithful householders invite a bhikkhu to take as much as he likes of robes, alms, food, resting places and medicinal requisites, the bhikkhu does not know moderation in accepting.

99
00:10:10,892 --> 00:10:19,341
So when we're visiting friends and family and they offer us biscuits, we have to be careful not to eat the whole packet.

100
00:10:20,782 --> 00:10:24,426
How does a bhikkhu show no extra veneration to those elders?

101
00:10:24,777 --> 00:10:30,865
Bhikkhus of long standing, who've long gone forth who are the fathers and leaders of the Sangha.

102
00:10:31,466 --> 00:10:40,380
Here a bhikkhu does not maintain bodily acts of loving kindness, both openly and privately, the same with verbal acts and the same with mental acts.

103
00:10:41,001 --> 00:10:44,506
And this is how a bhikkhu shows no extra veneration to the elders.

104
00:10:45,128 --> 00:10:53,620
So that's more specific to monks' relationships to relationship to the elders.

105
00:10:53,961 --> 00:10:56,926
But of course, it's just a general understanding.

106
00:10:57,527 --> 00:11:05,378
It's making a distinction between knowing somebody who is in authority as opposed to an authority.

107
00:11:05,899 --> 00:11:09,464
So when somebody is in authority, they are in authority over.

108
00:11:10,166 --> 00:11:11,827
So that might be your boss

109
00:11:13,681 --> 00:11:15,121
fear, of course.

110
00:11:15,802 --> 00:11:20,488
But if somebody is an authority, then you look up to them and you respect them.

111
00:11:20,748 --> 00:11:25,253
And it's acknowledging that, that you acknowledge this person's authority in any field of life.

112
00:11:25,373 --> 00:11:27,254
It doesn't matter if it's the Dharma or not.

113
00:11:28,596 --> 00:11:38,285
So when a Bhikkhu possesses these 11 qualities, which are all negative, he is incapable of growth, increase and fulfillment in this Dharma and discipline.

114
00:11:38,986 --> 00:11:41,730
So now the whole section now repeats it all.

115
00:11:42,351 --> 00:11:46,677
It repeats everything we've just been through, only on a positive note.

116
00:11:48,419 --> 00:12:00,956
So finally, the Buddha says, when a bhikkhu possesses these 11 qualities, he is capable of growth, increase and fulfillment in this dharma and discipline.

117
00:12:01,336 --> 00:12:08,746
This is what the Blessed One said, and the bhikkhus were satisfied and delighted in the Blessed One's words.

118
00:12:09,081 --> 00:12:12,106
So that's that particular discourse.

119
00:12:12,167 --> 00:12:21,722
Now, this is the beauty of this little book that I think I've shown you before, Pressing Out Pure Honey by Sharda Rajel.

120
00:12:22,124 --> 00:12:31,038
So here you see she puts those points very nicely for us, understanding that all material form of whatever kind,

121
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:40,543
Understanding that whether one is a fool or a wise person, one is characterized by one's actions.

122
00:12:41,304 --> 00:12:46,330
Abandoning desire, ill will and cruelty, all evil and wholesome states.

123
00:12:47,230 --> 00:12:55,759
Practicing restraint and guarding the sense doors and mind and mind objects so that greed and or aversion do not arise in the mind.

124
00:12:56,561 --> 00:13:00,705
Teaching others in detail the Dharma as oneself has learned and mastered it.

125
00:13:01,495 --> 00:13:29,240
going to learned ones and asking pertinent questions in order to delve into the meaning of the Dharma, gaining inspiration and gladness in the Dharma, understanding the Eightfold Path as it actually is, understanding the four foundations of mindfulness as they actually are, taking in moderation whatever is offered, maintaining loving-kindness, bodily, verbally and mentally, both openly and privately,

126
00:13:29,575 --> 00:13:33,240
to elders of long standing and to leaders of the Sangha.

127
00:13:36,504 --> 00:13:37,245
There we are.

128
00:13:37,625 --> 00:13:49,922
So I hope that that has been an inspiration of sorts and that it will encourage you to continue your practice and achieve full liberation sooner rather than later.

129
00:13:51,403 --> 00:13:53,506
So we can practice now a little bit ourselves.

